WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:04.580
As all the major TV networks announced their
pickups and cancellations for the upcoming

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:07.670
season, the biggest surprise came from ABC.

00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:12.840
Even though the Tim Allen show Last Man Standing
was the network's second highest-rated comedy,

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:16.119
ABC decided to drop the sitcom after six seasons.

00:00:16.119 --> 00:00:19.420
Why would they end one of their most successful
shows without warning?

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:22.640
Here are some of the reasons Last Man Standing
took a fall.

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:24.250
A major network shift

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:29.060
Though Last Man Standing aired on ABC, the
network didn't actually own the show.

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:34.120
The sitcom was produced by 20th Century Fox,
which meant ABC had to pay licensing fees

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:35.390
every season.

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:39.390
This may have factored into the cancelation
because it made the show more expensive than

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:41.000
some of their other comedies.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.810
Still, that may not be the whole story.

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:48.170
ABC's Fresh Off the Boat is also produced
by 20th Century Fox, but was renewed for a

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:50.880
fourth season despite lower ratings.

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:55.430
ABC Entertainment President Channing Dungey
said that axing Last Man Standing was simply

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:56.750
a business decision.

00:00:56.750 --> 00:01:00.040
The network decided to make Friday a night
for dramas.

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:04.889
And once the scheduling switch was made, they
felt Last Man Standing had no place to go.

00:01:04.889 --> 00:01:09.450
The show shared the night with Dr. Ken, which
was also canceled, though the Ken Jeong program

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:12.249
netted half as many viewers on an average
night.

00:01:12.249 --> 00:01:16.729
Dungey explained the difference, saying, "Last
Man Standing was a challenging one for me

00:01:16.729 --> 00:01:21.100
because it was a steady performer in the ratings,
but once we made the decision not to continue

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:23.990
with comedies on Fridays, that was where we
landed."

00:01:23.990 --> 00:01:30.159
Fridays will be all drama on ABC now, including
Once Upon a Time and Marvel's upcoming Inhumans

00:01:30.159 --> 00:01:31.289
series.

00:01:31.289 --> 00:01:32.969
Budgeting woes

00:01:32.969 --> 00:01:36.950
For a lot of shows, season seven is a year
of contract negotiations.

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:41.700
Last Man Standing was no exception: Tim Allen's
contract needed to be renewed, which more

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:44.180
than likely meant a pretty big raise.

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:48.999
Since the show made less money for ABC because
it was owned by Fox, and because Allen already

00:01:48.999 --> 00:01:53.539
had a pretty sizable salary, the network may
not have wanted to pump even more money into

00:01:53.539 --> 00:01:54.539
the sitcom.

00:01:54.539 --> 00:01:59.310
Sure, ratings were good, and good ratings
typically equal lots of network dollars.

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:03.219
But Last Man Standing also didn't have the
ideal audience.

00:02:03.219 --> 00:02:06.310
Advertisers want viewers in the 18 to 49 age
group.

00:02:06.310 --> 00:02:10.940
While the program did fairly well in that
demographic, the show's audience skewed older.

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:15.250
If advertisers weren't willing to shell out
the big bucks, ABC wasn't willing to foot

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:17.020
the growing bill.

00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:18.330
Playing politics?

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:22.780
After Last Man Standing's cancellation was
announced, rumor quickly spread that ABC pulled

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:26.220
the plug because of Allen's openly conservative
politics.

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:31.030
The show's premise rested on an old school
guy who rails against PC culture and wishes

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:33.180
we could go back to the good old days.

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:35.160
"Women want to have sports—sporting events
with men!

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:36.230
I don't get it.

00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:40.810
Because if you beat a woman you're a bully,
but if you lose to a woman you're an embarrassment."

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:44.620
Some suspect the network may have wanted to
distance themselves from that conservative

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:49.430
viewpoint, especially since Dungey has previously
said Donald Trump's presidency has made her

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:51.810
re-think the network's' programming slate.

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:56.480
"You'd think any woman would know the value
of being compared to a device like this.

00:02:57.920 --> 00:02:59.740
but no, no, no."

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:03.760
In real life, Allen is a proud Republican
and has stirred up some controversy with his

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:07.430
off-kilter comments about his status as a
rare conservative in Hollywood.

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:09.760
"You gotta be real careful around here.

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:12.760
You get beat up if you don't believe what
everyone believes.

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:14.580
This is like '30s Germany.

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:16.390
I don't know what happened."

00:03:16.390 --> 00:03:21.320
Wisconsin's Republican Governor Scott Walker
tweeted his support to Allen, stating "Looks

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:25.430
like ABC is playing politics with your show
despite decent ratings.

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:26.430
Sad."

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:31.290
Conservative pundit Glenn Beck chimed in during
his online radio show, vowing "to start looking

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:33.190
into why this show got canceled."

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:38.400
In response to the rumors, the network has
insisted politics played no part in Last Man

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:39.400
Standing's demise.

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:44.210
As ABC President Dungey put it, "I canceled
Last Man Standing for the same business and

00:03:44.210 --> 00:03:49.660
scheduling reasons I canceled The Real O'Neals,
Dr. Ken, The Catch, and American Crime."

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:54.180
Straightforward as that might sound, it did
nothing to stem the tide of fan outrage.

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:58.680
"When life knocks you down, you don't lie
on the canvas, crying like Al Gore after the

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:00.280
2000 election.

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:03.840
Boy, he blew up like the Hindenberg, didn't
he?"

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:04.840
Fighting back

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:09.090
Days after the cancellation was announced,
Tim Allen tweeted that he was "stunned and

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:13.940
blindsided by the network I called home for
six years," and his fans were just as irked.

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:18.470
A Change.org petition to save the show drew
more than a quarter of a million signatures

00:04:18.470 --> 00:04:21.900
of support during the days after the show's
fate was sealed.

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:26.139
Though the vocal support proves the show has
a fervent fanbase, its chances for finding

00:04:26.139 --> 00:04:27.580
a new home are low.

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:32.029
According to Deadline, Fox considered taking
the show, but decided they didn't have a place

00:04:32.029 --> 00:04:33.090
on their schedule.

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:37.889
The possibility of the show moving to streaming
services or other outlets is also reportedly

00:04:37.889 --> 00:04:38.889
remote.

00:04:38.889 --> 00:04:39.889
"Oh come on, Frank."

00:04:39.889 --> 00:04:42.919
"My husband will kick your ass first!"

00:04:42.919 --> 00:04:43.949
All of the above

00:04:43.949 --> 00:04:49.340
In the end, it looks like a number of different
factors played into Last Man Standing's surprising

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:50.340
cancellation.

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:54.250
ABC is rearranging their schedule and the
show was deceptively expensive — and to

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:58.469
think that politics had absolutely nothing
to do with it might be a bit of a stretch,

00:04:58.469 --> 00:05:00.000
despite the official line.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:04.219
Whether a boycott of the network or a fan
petition will ultimately have much impact

00:05:04.219 --> 00:05:05.400
remains to be seen.

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:08.849
"Protestors are rarely interested in facts,
and unfortunately we don't get picketed by

00:05:08.849 --> 00:05:10.520
angry historians."

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:15.710
For now at least, it looks like the Last Man
Standing probably won't get back up any time

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:16.710
soon...

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:17.710
Thanks for watching!

